	(text "Pins 1-32 copy the Digital Discovery's 2x16 DIN\nconnector (reference manual Fig. 8); 33/34 spare.\nA standard 34-way ribbon runs to a 2x16-to-34 adapter\nboard (pin n to pin n).\nDIN0-17 = the 18 bus lines in GPIO order (DB0..IO),\nDIN18/19 = the two markers, DIN20-23 unused.\nGND on 1, 2, 11, 12, 21, 22, 31, 32.\nEach tap has 100R at its receiver (channel sheets)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 100.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0026b47a-4ba8-555f-adb8-38449ecb8d42")
	)
	(text "SCSI: the same bus on both, wired by signal name from SCSI-2 Table 2 (IDC50 = contact set 1, HD50 = set 2)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 24.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1d78efbc-fa5a-5ae8-9cc6-f001b8175bcc")
	)
	(text "Receive-only lines"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 429.26 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2e0e22a2-2a81-5383-8dfa-18f712b49939")
	)
	(text "Connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "596c6cf0-76b5-5ae0-93e5-b10979bbe9a2")
	)
	(text "Active terminator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "63f0a51b-10af-5807-b5b7-1ca5a1bc6360")
	)
	(text "R301-R336: 220R 1 % 0402 (C25091), <= 35 mW each at 2.94 V into an asserted line.\nD301-D318: H5VUD5BB (C20615820), bidirectional, 0.3 pF, 5 V working. ESD protection: they clamp static\ndischarges from the cable or a finger on the connector to GND before they reach the FET or the receiver.\n0.3 pF keeps each line inside SCSI-2's 25 pF budget; bidirectional, so normal bus swings never make them conduct."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 33.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6df05260-b605-5b1e-994c-4fba0954305d")
	)
	(text "Pin 25 (HD50 13) is OPEN: a reversed ribbon puts TERMPWR on a\ndead pin, not on ground. IDC50 even pins 20, 22, 30, 34 are GROUND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 114.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "78081344-8ad6-5d77-b1af-644dce9e7bd0")
	)
	(text "SCSI-2 5.4.4: RESERVED lines 'shall be connected to ground' in end devices, 'should be open'\notherwise. We are an end device: all four fitted. Remove R337-R340 if the board ever sits mid-chain."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 151.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "81f809a7-a605-51c4-b5e9-5b2778c82c20")
	)
	(text "Per line: terminator pair (2 x 220R = 110R), ESD diode to GND, then the channel sheet (driver + receiver).\nKeep each cluster on its own bus trace by the connector. GATE (from the RP2350) and RX (to it) are sheet pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 24.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8a217d56-07c4-5c96-8a45-8ab2f2089f82")
	)
	(text "Switch state survives power-off and needs no firmware; DIP 2 lets firmware (expander P12) override it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 309.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9257fef4-8d93-50ad-8477-a9583ed20007")
	)
	(text "A1-A8 and DIR tie straight to the rail: DIR high = A->B, and bus-hold inputs mustn't get pull resistors.\nB7/B8 unused."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 281.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "95612034-b4d3-5f16-a396-057d247cc194")
	)
	(text "Terminator enable DIP switch"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 304.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a1d5ff5c-34c4-5984-8640-79b3c1fef33d")
	)
	(text "J303 logic-analyzer header (Digital Discovery DIN)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 36.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b4fbb079-7207-5593-a85d-30d030b8ec03")
	)
	(text "TERMINATOR_EN_INVERTED drives /OE on U301-U303: low = terminated. R341 pulls it up to\n2.83 V (off). DIP 1 closes it to GND through R342: ~0.26 V = on. DIP 2 connects it to\nthe expander pin (push-pull, so it can override R342). The expander powers up with its\npins as inputs, so the switch default holds; firmware reads the pin to learn it.\nMid-chain and possibly unpowered: use off/off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 372.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c5044526-e802-57f6-804d-c920ce6f702f")
	)
	(text "J302 SCSI HD50 (DNP)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 36.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c55e0f2d-b48e-59e5-b3dd-353ad56ff1e1")
	)
	(text "MSG, C/D, REQ, I/O: only the target drives them (SCSI-2 Table 6), so no driver."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 429.26 197.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e50459e3-3547-586e-a0ca-98fcbb6135aa")
	)
	(text "VTERMINATOR (2.83 V) -> SN74LVTH245A, A tied high -> TERMINATOR_OUT_<line> -> 2 x 220R per line (next to each line,\nright) -> bus. /OE high or unpowered: outputs high-Z. 6 lines per package, in connector order."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 184.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ede5b533-0b5f-50ee-ba59-5481a6590c2f")
	)
	(text "Per-line driver and receiver"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.7 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f0d79e0d-386c-5aad-bc2d-54aaca569ab9")
	)
	(text "J301 SCSI IDC50 (fitted)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 36.83 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f7c8a322-3f4e-5c49-b53e-5ca3935fefe1")
	)
